## Context
Author's ruling 2026-10-27 on the flows note (conception/2026-10-27-review-merge-flows.md, PR #1809): F1 is the
default (review on notes, merge by forge PR); F2, the local gated merge, is only for repositories without an
upstream. No setting. Today scripts/forge.py get_forge in auto mode selects the local merge whenever gh is absent
or the ref is not numeric, so a repository with an origin lands locally when gh is missing.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] With a remote named origin, landing never selects the local merge: without gh it refuses, naming the cause.
- [ ] With no origin remote, landing selects the local gated merge; review on notes is unchanged in both cases.
- [ ] The IDH_FORGE environment switch is removed or reduced to test-only use, stated in the code; tests cover both cases.
- [ ] The harness gate passes (full make check, including the integration tier).

